## 3. Features to ADD — Making it an Autonomous Research Assistant

Based on your recommendations and analysis, here's the transformation plan:

### 🔴 Priority 1: Core Intelligence Upgrades

#### A. Full Paper Extraction (Your Recommendation #1)
**Current:** Gap agent only sees first 200 chars of abstracts.
**Proposed:**
- Wire `pdf_extractor.py` into the retrieval pipeline
- After paper retrieval, run `extract_full_text()` for top-ranked papers
- Store full text in `PaperCache` model (already exists but unused)
- Feed full text to gap_agent, idea_agent, and writer_agent
- Add a "full text status" indicator on the papers page

#### B. Replace Code Page with Detailed Report & PPT Page (Your Recommendation #2)
**Current:** Step 6 generates ML boilerplate code — not useful for all research.
**Proposed:**
- **Remove** the code generation step entirely
- **Replace with** a "Research Guide" page that generates:
  - **Detailed Project Report**: How to build the project, methodology walkthrough, tools to use, research methods, tech stack recommendations, related work deep-dive
  - **Presentation Deck**: Auto-generated slide content (title, problem, methodology, expected results, timeline, references) — exportable as PPTX
  - **Tool Recommendations**: Specific software, libraries, datasets, compute resources based on the idea
  - **Research Methodology Guide**: Step-by-step guide on HOW to execute the research (data collection methods, experiment design, statistical analysis)

#### C. Enhanced Execution Plan (Your Recommendation #3)
**Current:** Basic phases list with a simple tech stack.
**Proposed:**
- **Dynamic Gantt-style timeline** with dependencies between tasks
- **Resource allocation**: Compute requirements, dataset sizes, storage needs
- **Milestone checkpoints** with go/no-go criteria
- **Risk mitigation strategies** for each identified risk
- **Literature review plan**: Which papers to read first and why
- **Collaboration tools**: Recommended tools for version control, experiment tracking, paper writing
- **Budget estimation**: Compute costs, API costs, dataset licensing

### 🟡 Priority 2: Autonomous Continuous Operation (Like OpenCode)

#### D. Auto-Pipeline Mode
- One-click "Run Full Analysis" — automatically executes all 7 steps in sequence
- Real-time progress dashboard showing which agent is running
- Streaming output for each step visible simultaneously
- Auto-retry with fallback on failures

#### E. Research Chat / Q&A Agent
- Chat interface that can answer questions about the retrieved papers, gaps, and ideas
- Uses RAG over the full paper texts
- Can refine research direction mid-pipeline
- Remembers conversation context across sessions

#### F. Iterative Refinement Loop
- After seeing results, user can provide feedback
- System re-runs relevant agents with updated context
- "Deep dive" button on any gap or idea → spawns a sub-research task

### 🟢 Priority 3: Quality & Polish

#### G. Paper Source Improvements
- Add Google Scholar, DBLP, CrossRef as sources
- Full-text PDF download and storage
- Citation graph visualization
- Paper recommendation engine ("papers like this one")

#### H. Export Improvements
- LaTeX export (not just DOCX/PDF)
- BibTeX reference export
- PPTX presentation export
- Notion/Obsidian markdown export

#### I. UI/UX Improvements
- Dark/light theme toggle (infrastructure exists in `useThemeStore`)
- Progress indicators showing pipeline completion percentage
- Keyboard shortcuts for navigation
- Mobile responsive layout
- Real-time collaboration (WebSocket)

